@ 17.2.3 - Common Anatolian to Lycian
# citation: Alces, from http://www.unc.edu/~melchert/anathistphon.pdf (link is dead) “[P]lus lots of syncope which he doesn’t elaborate on”
	D > T / #_
	D > F:[+voice]
	N{F:[+voice],T} > nD
	d > k / _w
	kʷ > t / _E
	kʷ > k / _E, in Milyan
	{ɡ́,ɡ} > j / _{ e, e:[+long] }
	{ɡ́,ɡ} > ∅ / _{ i, i:[+long] }
	ɡ > ∅ / V_V
	j > ∅ / ts_
	s > z / _{R,j,w} “(in Milyan, this happened after the change of ḱ to s)”
	s > h
	ḱ > s
	ɣʷ > ɡ / _B
	x > k / E_E (probably a palatal stop)
	x > q / _E (possibly plain velar stop)
	x > x / else (possibly a uvular stop)
	w > b / C_
	ɡ > dʒ (sporadic)
	e > i / j_
	{ɛ,e}:[+long] o æ:[+long] > i:[+long] e a:[+long]
	V:[+long] > V:[-long]
	e > a / _U:[+u, a]
	a > e / _U:[+e, i]